<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha taught that when mindfulness of the body is developed and cultivated, <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.586/en/sujato"><b>ignorance</b></a> is abandoned? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.586/en/sujato">AN 1.586</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha explained that the cultivation of mindfulness of the body is what causes <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.587/en/sujato"><b>true knowledge</b></a> to arise in the practitioner? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.587/en/sujato">AN 1.587</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha identified mindfulness of the body as the key practice for the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.588/en/sujato"><b>abandoning of the conceit 'I am'</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.588/en/sujato">AN 1.588</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that according to the Buddha, mindfulness of the body is the means by which the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.589/en/sujato"><b>underlying tendencies</b></a> are uprooted? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.589/en/sujato">AN 1.589</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha taught that by frequently practicing mindfulness of the body, all <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.590/en/sujato"><b>fetters</b></a> are eventually abandoned? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.590/en/sujato">AN 1.590</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha taught that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.596/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a>, when developed and cultivated, is the one thing that leads to the realization of the fruit of stream-entry? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.596/en/sujato">AN 1.596</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha stated that the singular practice of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.597/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a>, when practiced frequently, leads to the realization of the fruit of once-returning? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.597/en/sujato">AN 1.597</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that according to the Buddha, <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.598/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a> is the one quality that, when developed and cultivated, leads to the realization of the fruit of non-returning? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.598/en/sujato">AN 1.598</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha identified <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.599/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a> as the one thing that, when developed and cultivated, leads to the realization of the fruit of arahantship? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.599/en/sujato">AN 1.599</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha taught that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.600/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a> is the single thing that leads to the acquisition of wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.600/en/sujato">AN 1.600</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha encouraged the development of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.601/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a> because it leads to the growth of wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.601/en/sujato">AN 1.601</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha explained that the practice of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.602/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a> leads to the expansion of wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.602/en/sujato">AN 1.602</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha claimed that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.603/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a>, when practiced frequently, leads to the attainment of great wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.603/en/sujato">AN 1.603</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha taught that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.604/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a> is the one practice that leads to wide wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.604/en/sujato">AN 1.604</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha said that cultivating <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.605/en/sujato"><b>mindfulness directed to the body</b></a> leads to the achievement of abundant wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an1.605/en/sujato">AN 1.605</a></p></div><hr>
