<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha highlighted that being <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an10.53/en/sujato"><b>doubtful</b></a> is a hindrance that a monk must cross over through diligent and systematic self-examination? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an10.53/en/sujato">AN 10.53</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha said that if a monk discovers he is <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an10.53/en/sujato"><b>angry</b></a>, he should apply extraordinary desire and effort to abandon that anger, just as if his own clothes were on fire? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an10.53/en/sujato">AN 10.53</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha used the imagery of someone with their <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an10.53/en/sujato"><b>head on fire</b></a> to illustrate the extreme urgency and "unremitting mindfulness" required to abandon unwholesome mental states? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/an10.53/en/sujato">AN 10.53</a></p></div><hr>
