<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato"><b>Venerable Mahā-Moggallāna</b></a> rebuked the monk Potthila for being "empty" of spiritual substance while being overly attached to his own fame and status? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato">Thag 20.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato"><b>Venerable Mahā-Moggallāna</b></a> compared a monk who is infatuated with fame and unwholesome deeds to a worm that wallows in dung? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato">Thag 20.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato"><b>Venerable Mahā-Moggallāna</b></a> described Venerable Sāriputta as a beautiful and liberated sage who serves as an unsurpassed field of merit for the world? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato">Thag 20.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato"><b>Venerable Mahā-Moggallāna</b></a> was honored by ten thousand Brahmas who stood with joined palms to pay him homage as a "supreme person"? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thag20.1/en/sujato">Thag 20.1</a></p></div><hr>
