<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Rohiṇī</b> advised her father to accept and maintain the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato"><b>moral precepts</b></a> as a foundation for his future happiness? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato">Thig 13.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Rohiṇī</b> described the speech of recluses as being both <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato"><b>wise and humble</b></a>, reflecting their inner peace? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato">Thig 13.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Rohiṇī</b>'s father eventually declared that his household had become a site for a great <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato"><b>spiritual sacrifice</b></a> through his hospitality toward the recluses? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato">Thig 13.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Rohiṇī</b> emphasized that recluses have <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato"><b>cleansed all evil</b></a> from their hearts, making them worthy of the highest respect? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato">Thig 13.2</a></p></div><hr>
