<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Rohiṇī</b> was allowed to ordain and renounce the world only after her parents had <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato"><b>accepted the Dhamma</b></a> themselves? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato">Thig 13.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Rohiṇī</b>'s father described his final attainment as a state of being <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato"><b>safe and secure</b></a> from the dangers of the cycle of birth and death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.2/en/sujato">Thig 13.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā was praised by the Buddha as the foremost among his female disciples who were <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>preachers</b></a> of the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā decided to seek ordination after her husband, Visākha, attained the level of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>Non-Returner</b></a> and ceased his worldly interactions with her? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā was born into a prominent family in <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>Rājagaha</b></a> before renouncing the household life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā chose to live in a secluded village monastery where she mastered the four <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>analytical knowledges</b></a> and attained Arahantship? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā traveled to the community of nuns to be ordained while riding in a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>golden palanquin</b></a> provided by her husband? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā defined a person as being <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>bound upstream</b></a> if they have a mind filled with a desire for the "Undetermined" and are no longer caught by sensual pleasures? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā taught that reaching the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>Undetermined</b></a> state (Nirvana) requires one to have an mind that is completely unattached to the world of desires? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā was so skilled in explaining the Dhamma that she was the primary speaker in the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>Cūḷavedalla Sutta</b></a>, where she answered deep questions for her former husband? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā described the spiritual path as one where the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>desire for the unborn</b></a> state must be so pervasive that it occupies the entire mind? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā attained liberation by practicing <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>seclusion</b></a>, preferring a quiet village retreat over the busy surroundings of her hometown? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammadinnā emphasized that a mind <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato"><b>not bound</b></a> by sensual pleasures is a prerequisite for being called a "higher streamer" on the path to awakening? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.12/en/sujato">Thig 1.12</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Visākhā encouraged her fellow monastics to strictly <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato"><b>follow the instructions</b></a> of the Buddha to ensure they would never experience remorse? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato">Thig 1.13</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Visākhā achieved <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato"><b>Arahantship</b></a> and subsequently shared her deep spiritual insights to inspire her companions to continue their practice? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato">Thig 1.13</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Visākhā advised her fellow nuns that after completing their duties, they should <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato"><b>wash their feet</b></a> and sit down quietly to focus on their meditation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato">Thig 1.13</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Visākhā attained the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato"><b>bliss of liberation</b></a> and proclaimed her final knowledge to help others along the same spiritual path? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato">Thig 1.13</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Visākhā taught that those who <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato"><b>act properly</b></a> according to the Dhamma will live a life free from the burden of future regret? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.13/en/sujato">Thig 1.13</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā was told by the Buddha to view the various elements of existence as <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato"><b>suffering</b></a> in order to avoid returning to the cycle of rebirth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato">Thig 1.14</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā was exhorted to give up her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato"><b>desire for existence</b></a> so that she could live a life of total peace and tranquility? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato">Thig 1.14</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha appeared in a vision before Bhikkhuni Sumānā to urge her to never go back into the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato"><b>path of rebirth</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato">Thig 1.14</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā described her final state of spiritual attainment as being <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato"><b>cool and extinguished</b></a>, free from the heat of all defilements? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.14/en/sujato">Thig 1.14</a></p></div><hr>
