<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Uttarā attained a state of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.15/en/sujato"><b>profound stillness</b></a> after bringing all her mental and physical faculties under complete control? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.15/en/sujato">Thig 1.15</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā was born into a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>noble family</b></a> in the city of Rājagaha before she chose to renounce the world and seek liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā decided to ordain after being deeply moved by a sermon given by the eminent <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>Dhammadinnā</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā attained the state of an Arahant and gained profound <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>analytical knowledge</b></a> after dedicated practice in insight meditation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā became a renowned teacher who was often accompanied and supported by a community of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>five hundred bhikkhunis</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā's teaching was described as being so sweet and nourishing that her listeners felt as though they were receiving <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>honey</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā's words were said to be permeated with the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>deathless</b></a>, causing her audience to sit in complete and devoted silence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>tree deity</b></a> was so moved by the preaching of Bhikkhuni Sukkā that the spirit went into the streets of Rājagaha to praise her? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā was defended by a spirit who scolded the citizens for acting as if they were <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>asleep</b></a> while such a profound teacher spoke the Buddha's word? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā's Dhamma was compared by a deity to a stream of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>pure water</b></a> that is unobstructed and refreshing to a weary traveler? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā was addressed by a spirit as a "child of the light" who had attained a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>stabilization of mind</b></a> that was completely free from lust? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā reached her final goal after having defeated <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>Mara's army</b></a>, signifying her total victory over all mental defilements? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā declared she was bearing her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>final body</b></a>, a term indicating she had successfully ended the cycle of rebirth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā's preaching caused such a great <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>stir among the people</b></a> that they began to flock to the monastery specifically to hear her speak? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā initially became a devoted <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>lay follower</b></a> in her own home before choosing to enter the monastic order? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā's name means <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>bright or pure</b></a>, reflecting her spiritual clarity and her attainment of the highest wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā achieved her liberation through the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>light of the Dhamma</b></a>, which allowed her to see the true nature of reality? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sukkā reached a state where she was completely <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato"><b>freed from passion</b></a>, having dried up the roots of craving and suffering within herself? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.6/en/sujato">Thig 3.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā was born into a Brahmin family in the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>Sāvatthī</b></a> and first became a lay follower when the Buddha accepted the donation of the Jetavana monastery? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā was inspired to renounce the world and enter the homeless life after hearing a sermon delivered by an <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>Arahant</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha praised Bhikkhunī Sakulā as being the foremost among all the nuns in the possession of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>divine eye</b></a> (dibbacakkhu)? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that while she was still a laywoman living at home, Bhikkhunī Sakulā saw the stainless Dhamma and the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>deathless Nibbāna</b></a>, which prompted her spiritual journey? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā chose to abandon her sons, daughters, and all her accumulated <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>wealth and grain</b></a> to shave her hair and go forth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that during her time as a trainee (sikkhamānā), Bhikkhunī Sakulā diligently developed the path to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>abandon lust and hatred</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā achieved a state where she could <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>recollect her past lives</b></a> after she received higher ordination and refined her spiritual practice? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā attained a state of coolness and peace by realizing that all external objects are <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>conditioned and perishable</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā focused her training on the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>gradual destruction</b></a> of her mental taints (āsavas) until she was completely liberated? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā described her mind as being <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>quenched and peaceful</b></a> after she successfully uprooted every single mental corruption? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā emphasized the importance of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>homeless life</b></a> as the proper environment for developing the path to enlightenment? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā achieved a state where her divine eye was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>completely stainless</b></a> and well-cultivated through her intense meditative efforts? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sakulā used the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato"><b>straight path</b></a> of the Buddha’s teaching to systematically remove the stains of the mind? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.7/en/sujato">Thig 5.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā was born into a noble family in Sāvatthī and was nicknamed "<a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>Many Children</b></a>" because she had ten sons and daughters? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā decided to go forth as a nun after she was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>disrespected and neglected</b></a> by her own children and daughters-in-law following the distribution of her wealth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that despite her advanced age when she ordained, Bhikkhunī Sonā was praised by the Buddha as being foremost in the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>faculty of energy</b></a> (viriya)? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that to prevent herself from falling or hitting her head while practicing in the dark, Bhikkhunī Sonā would navigate the monastery by holding onto <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>porch posts and tree branches</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha appeared to Bhikkhunī Sonā in a vision of light and taught her that one day of seeing the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>deathless state</b></a> is superior to a hundred years of life in ignorance? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā's spiritual progress was guided by another nun who taught her the Dhamma concerning the aggregates, the sense bases, and the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>elements of existence</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā attained final liberation by developing a one-pointed mind through the practice of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>signless meditation</b></a> (animitta)? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā declared that she had successfully <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>uprooted the five aggregates</b></a> and cut the very root of craving, ensuring no further rebirth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā's husband left the household life to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>ordain as a monk</b></a> before she eventually decided to follow the same path? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā described her aging physical body as a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>heap of suffering</b></a> that had become weak after raising her ten children? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā attained the purification of her divine eye and gained the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>knowledge of her past lives</b></a> by following her teacher's instructions? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā attained a state of peace that was free from any <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>clinging or attachment</b></a> after she realized the truth of the aggregates? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā became a symbol of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>unwavering persistence</b></a> for her ability to serve the community of nuns while maintaining an intensive meditation schedule? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Sonā confirmed that she had <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato"><b>reached the highest fruit</b></a> of the spiritual life, meaning she had nothing more left to do for her liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato">Thig 5.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā was born in the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>Sāvatthī</b></a> into a family of domestic slaves serving in the household of the famous benefactor Anāthapiṇḍika? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā attained the first stage of enlightenment, known as <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>Stream-entry</b></a> (Sotāpanna), immediately after listening to the Buddha preach the "Lion's Roar" discourse? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā successfully converted a Brahmin to the Buddha’s path by logically refuting his belief that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>ritual bathing</b></a> in a river could cleanse a person of their bad kamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā was granted her formal release from <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>slavery</b></a> by her master after she helped convert a Brahmin, allowing her to ordain as a nun with his full support? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā attained final liberation as an Arahant together with the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>analytical knowledges</b></a> (paṭisambhidā) of the Dhamma and its meaning? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that before her ordination, Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā was required to carry water from the river daily, even during the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>cold of winter</b></a>, for the household she served? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā performed her difficult water-carrying duties out of a deep-seated <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>fear of punishment</b></a> and the verbal reproaches of her mistresses? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā challenged a shivering Brahmin she saw in the river, asking him why he chose to suffer the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>freezing cold</b></a> when he was not a slave forced to be there? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā pointed out the absurdity of ritual purification by stating that if water washed away sins, then <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>frogs and turtles</b></a> would all be destined for heaven? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā argued that if a river could wash away an individual’s bad deeds, it would logically also wash away all of their <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>good deeds</b></a> as well? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā mocked the Brahmin’s belief in water-cleansing by suggesting that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>crocodiles and water-snakes</b></a> would be the most purified of all living beings? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā reasoned that even the most violent <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>criminals and hunters</b></a> could easily free themselves from their evil actions if simple immersion in water were truly effective? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā advised the Brahmin to stop his ritual bathing so that he could prevent the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>extreme cold</b></a> from further damaging his physical health? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that when the Brahmin, out of gratitude, offered Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>soaked robe</b></a> as a gift, she declined it, as she was not seeking material reward for her advice? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā warned the Brahmin that if he truly disliked suffering, he should refrain from committing <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>evil deeds</b></a> whether they were done openly or in secret? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā taught that a person cannot escape from the experience of suffering simply by <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>running away</b></a> if they continue to perform unwholesome actions? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā encouraged the former Brahmin to take the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>Triple Refuge</b></a> in the Buddha, the Dhamma, and the Sangha to find true spiritual security? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā urged the Brahmin to formally accept the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>five precepts</b></a> of moral conduct as a way to secure his own future welfare? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that under the guidance of Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā, the Brahmin eventually entered the monkhood and attained the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>Three Knowledges</b></a> (tevijjā) of an Arahant? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā was recognized by the former Brahmin as the person who had pointed him away from a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>false path</b></a> and toward the Noble Path of the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā attained a state where her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>mind was gote-sạch</b></a> (cleansed) and purified, reaching the highest goal of the spiritual life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Brahmin converted by Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā formerly prided himself on being a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>relative of Brahma</b></a> by birth but later realized his true nobility through spiritual attainment? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā identified the Buddha’s teaching on the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>Lion's Roar</b></a> as the catalyst for her initial understanding of the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā used her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>analytical insight</b></a> into the teaching to compose and repeat the verses describing her victory over spiritual ignorance? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the verses attributed to Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā in the Therīgāthā were considered so profound that the monk she converted later <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>repeated them</b></a> to reflect on his own attainment? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Puṇṇā’s life story serves as a powerful example that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato"><b>spiritual liberation</b></a> is accessible to all human beings, regardless of their gender or social standing? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig12.1/en/sujato">Thig 12.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> was the daughter of a hunter chief in the village of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Vankahāra</b></a> before she eventually renounced the world to join the Order? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b>, an ascetic named Upaka, first encountered the Buddha on the road between the Bodhi tree and <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Bārāṇasī</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that when the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> asked the Buddha who his teacher was, the Buddha declared that he was the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Conqueror of All</b></a> and had no teacher? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha told the future husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> that he was going to Bārāṇasī to beat the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>drum of the Deathless</b></a> for the sake of the world? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> was of such striking beauty that the ascetic Upaka became so infatuated with her that he <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>refused to eat</b></a> until her father agreed to their marriage? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> gave up his life as an ascetic to become a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>seller of game</b></a> caught by her father and brothers? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> bore a son named <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Subhadda</b></a>, whose name she used to mock her husband's former life as a recluse? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> used to tease her husband while nursing their child by calling the boy the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>son of an ascetic</b></a> who had become a mere laborer? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> eventually decided to leave his family to seek out his "friend," the Buddha, after becoming fed up with her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>constant mockery</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> once pleaded with her husband not to be angry with her, calling him a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>great hero</b></a> in an attempt to keep him from renouncing their life together? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> warned her husband that an ascetic who is overcome by <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>anger</b></a> cannot truly succeed in his spiritual practice? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> tried to lure her husband back to household life by promising that she and her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>entire family</b></a> would be subservient to his wishes? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> compared her own youthful beauty to a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>pomegranate tree</b></a> in full bloom on a mountain peak to entice her husband to stay? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> described herself as wearing the finest <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Kāsī silk</b></a> and being perfumed with red sandalwood while trying to prevent her husband's departure? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> rejected her advances by comparing her beauty to a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>fowler's snare</b></a> meant to trap a bird? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that in a moment of desperation, <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> threatened to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>harm her own son</b></a> with a staff or a knife if her husband did not return to her? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> remained unmoved by her threats, stating that even if she threw the child to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>wolves or dogs</b></a>, he would not return to the household life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> compared his renunciation to a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>mighty elephant</b></a> breaking its bonds to find freedom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> eventually realized the depth of her husband's resolve and asked him which <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>city or capital</b></a> he intended to travel to? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> was told by her husband that he was going to see the Buddha, who was teaching the Dhamma on the banks of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Nirañjarā River</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> requested her husband to pay homage to the Buddha on her behalf and to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>circumambulate</b></a> him out of respect? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha, knowing the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> was coming, instructed his monks to welcome any traveler who asked for the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Vanquisher of Death</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> attained the fruit of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Non-returner</b></a> (anāgāmī) soon after meeting the Buddha in Sāvatthī? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that after her husband left, <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> entrusted her son to his grandfather and left her home in <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Nāḷā</b></a> to seek ordination? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> successfully attained the state of an Arahant and realized the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>three knowledges</b></a> (tevijjā) after following the path shown by the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> praised the Buddha for teaching the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Four Noble Truths</b></a>, which lead to the complete ending of suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> specifically mentioned the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Eightfold Path</b></a> as the way that leads to the cessation of all painful states? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> eventually understood that her attachment to her family was a form of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>bondage</b></a> from which she needed to be liberated? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> acknowledged that before hearing the Dhamma, she and her husband lived in a way that was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>not according to the Dhamma</b></a>, despite their outward appearances? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> ultimately found peace by recognizing the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>origin of suffering</b></a> and letting go of her worldly desires? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b>'s verses record her transformation from a woman using her beauty as a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>decoy</b></a> to a liberated nun who had fulfilled the Buddha's teachings? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the husband of <b>Bhikkhunī Cāpā</b> was reborn in the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato"><b>Aviha heaven</b></a>, where he eventually attained final Arahantship? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.3/en/sujato">Thig 13.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā, the elder sister of King Kosala, had to delay her ordination for many years because she was dedicated to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato"><b>caring for her grandmother</b></a> until the latter's passing? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato">Thig 1.16</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā was first inspired to seek the Triple Refuge after hearing the Buddha teach that there are <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato"><b>four young things</b></a>—a prince, a snake, a fire, and a monk—which should never be despised? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato">Thig 1.16</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā attained the stage of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato"><b>Non-Returner</b></a> as a laywoman after donating numerous screens and cloths to the Sangha and hearing a sermon by the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato">Thig 1.16</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha addressed Bhikkhuni Sumānā as an "<a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato"><b>old nun</b></a>" and encouraged her to sleep in peace, wrapped in the robe that she had made for herself? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato">Thig 1.16</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā achieved the final goal of Arahantship and became <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato"><b>cool and quenched</b></a> the moment her greed and lust were completely stilled? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato">Thig 1.16</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā repeated the verse originally spoken to her by the Buddha as her own <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato"><b>declaration of final knowledge</b></a> after realizing the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato">Thig 1.16</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sumānā was a resident of the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato"><b>Sāvatthī</b></a> and used the wealth and influence of her royal family to support the Buddha's community before ordaining in her old age? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.16/en/sujato">Thig 1.16</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammā was born into a distinguished family but was only able to enter the monastic life after her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato"><b>husband passed away</b></a>, as he had previously refused her request to ordain? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato">Thig 1.17</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammā attained total liberation of the heart after <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato"><b>falling to the ground</b></a> while returning from her almsround in a state of physical exhaustion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato">Thig 1.17</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammā used the experience of her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato"><b>trembling limbs</b></a> and failing strength as a subject for meditation to gain deep insight into the nature of existence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato">Thig 1.17</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammā was leaning on a staff for support when she collapsed, an event that led her to clearly see the inherent <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato"><b>danger of the body</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato">Thig 1.17</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammā achieved the state of an Arahant with the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato"><b>discrimination of the meaning</b></a> and the teachings through her focused contemplation of impermanence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato">Thig 1.17</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhammā expressed her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato"><b>spiritual joy</b></a> through a verse after her heart was liberated from all bonds at the very moment she fell? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.17/en/sujato">Thig 1.17</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Saṅghā chose to abandon her home, her children, and her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato"><b>precious livestock</b></a> to pursue the homeless life of a renunciant? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato">Thig 1.18</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Saṅghā successfully abandoned both <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato"><b>greed and hatred</b></a> as she cultivated the Path to reach the highest peace? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato">Thig 1.18</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Saṅghā practiced <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato"><b>seclusion from ignorance</b></a>, living a life of detachment until she attained her final spiritual victory? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato">Thig 1.18</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Saṅghā declared she had become <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato"><b>cool and still</b></a> after completely destroying the deep-seated roots of craving? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato">Thig 1.18</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Saṅghā described her ultimate state as being <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato"><b>extinguished</b></a>, signifying the total cessation of the fires of defilement and suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato">Thig 1.18</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Saṅghā’s spiritual journey involved <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato"><b>conquering craving</b></a> at its very origin, allowing her to live a life of profound tranquility? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.18/en/sujato">Thig 1.18</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā was originally a princess from the country of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>Āḷavī</b></a> before she followed her father’s example and entered the monastic life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā chose to renounce her royal status and ordain after her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>father</b></a>, the King of Āḷavī, was converted by the Buddha and became a monk? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā was once confronted by <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>Māra</b></a>, the Evil One, who appeared to her in the form of a stranger while she was seeking seclusion for her midday rest? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā was challenged by the Evil One with the claim that there is no <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>escape from the world</b></a>, as he attempted to shake her confidence in the path of renunciation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā was encouraged by Māra to abandon her solitude and <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>enjoy sensual pleasures</b></a> while she was still in the prime of her youth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā compared worldly sensual pleasures to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>swords and spears</b></a>, noting that they only serve to hack and destroy the five aggregates? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā declared that what the world considers "delight" held <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>no attraction</b></a> for her because she had completely uprooted all craving for existence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā successfully shattered the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>mass of darkness</b></a> of ignorance through the development of wisdom and insight into the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā attained liberation by subduing her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>bodily, verbal, and mental activities</b></a> and reaching the state of an Arahant? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā recognized her invisible opponent and boldly proclaimed that Māra was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>defeated</b></a> once she realized he was trying to disturb her peace? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā was the daughter of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>priestly chaplain</b></a> to King Bimbisāra of Magadha before she attained enlightenment as a female disciple of the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā was practicing meditation under a tree in the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>Blind Men’s Grove</b></a> near Sāvatthī when the Evil One attempted to disrupt her solitary rest? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā was taunted with the sexist claim that women possess only <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>two-fingered wisdom</b></a> and thus cannot reach the heights of spiritual attainment? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā countered gender-based prejudices by stating that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>womanhood</b></a> is no obstacle to enlightenment when the mind is well-composed? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā asked what difference it makes to be a woman when one is <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>insightfully perceiving the Dhamma</b></a> with a focused and wise mind? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā declared that her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>delight in everything</b></a> had been uprooted, signifying her total victory over all forms of craving and attachment? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā warned the tempter that he was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>defeated</b></a> because she had already torn asunder the mass of gloom that signifies spiritual ignorance? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā attained the state of an Arahant through the dedicated practice of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>insight meditation</b></a> and the full realization of the Four Noble Truths? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā faced Māra while he remained <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>invisible</b></a> to her, yet she still identified his intent to prevent her from enjoying the bliss of Nibbāna? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā was initially a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>laywoman</b></a> who accompanied her father to hear the Dhamma before she chose to seek full ordination in the Sangha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Selā told the Evil One that his description of sensual "pleasures" was actually an invitation to be <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato"><b>chopped to pieces</b></a> by suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.7/en/sujato">Thig 3.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā emphasized that spiritual realization depends solely on having a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>mind that is well-composed</b></a> and a heart free from defilements? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Somā used her rebuttal against Māra to show that the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato"><b>noble fruit</b></a> of the Buddha’s path is accessible to all who practice with diligence and wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig3.8/en/sujato">Thig 3.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā was born as the daughter of a wealthy <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>treasurer in Rājagaha</b></a> before she eventually renounced the world to seek spiritual liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā fell in love with a thief named Satthuka and persuaded her father to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>bribe the executioners</b></a> to save the criminal from being put to death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā was lured to the "Robber's Cliff" by her husband, who intended to kill her and <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>steal her jewelry</b></a> shortly after they were married? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā used her wit to save her own life by requesting a final embrace of her husband, which she used as an opportunity to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>push him off a cliff</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that a deity witnessed Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā outsmarting the thief and declared that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>wisdom is not exclusive</b></a> to men, as a clever woman can show even greater insight? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā first entered the homeless life by joining the Niganthas, an ascetic sect that required her to have her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>hair plucked out</b></a> by a palmyra comb? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the name of Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā refers to her "<a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>curly hair</b></a>," which grew back in tight curls after she had it removed during her initial ascetic training? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā became a formidable debater who would place a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>rose-apple branch</b></a> in a mound of sand at the entrance of a village as a challenge to anyone who dared to argue with her? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā met her spiritual match in the Venerable Sāriputta, who accepted her challenge by ordering children to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>trample the sand mound</b></a> she had built? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that during a public debate in Sāvatthī, Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā exhausted her entire repertoire of questions before the Venerable Sāriputta asked her a single question: "<a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>What is one?</b></a>" <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā admitted defeat when she could not answer Sāriputta's question and subsequently decided to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>seek refuge</b></a> in the Buddha's teaching? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā attained Arahantship immediately after the Buddha recited a verse stating that one <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>meaningful word</b></a> that brings peace is better than a thousand useless verses? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā received her higher ordination directly from the Buddha when he addressed her with the simple words, "<a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>Come, Bhaddā</b></a>"? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā recalled a time in her past when she wandered with only <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>one garment</b></a> and her body smeared with mud, holding many wrong views? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā traveled through the regions of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>Aṅga, Magadha, and Vajjī</b></a>, as well as the kingdom of Kosala, while practicing the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā lived for fifteen years as a "debtless" wanderer, meaning she consumed the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>alms-food of the land</b></a> without the burden of spiritual obligation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā encountered the Buddha on <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>Vulture's Peak Mountain</b></a> (Gijjhakūṭa) and paid homage to him before receiving his formal recognition? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā expressed her gratitude toward a wise lay follower who provided her with a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>robe</b></a>, which she used after being freed from all mental bonds? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā initially struggled with <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>distinguishing right from wrong</b></a>, viewing faults where there were none and failing to see faults where they actually existed? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā spent her days at the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>nun's monastery</b></a> (bhikkhunī-upassaya) living in bliss and happiness after achieving total liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā reached a state where she was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>free from all fetters</b></a> (saṃyojana), indicating she had completely eradicated the causes of suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā was known for her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>quick wit</b></a>, a trait the Buddha recognized as having matured into deep spiritual wisdom? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā was described as having a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>stain-free mind</b></a> after she bowed to the Buddha and received his teaching? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā had to leave her home because she felt she <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>could not return</b></a> after the traumatic event of killing her husband at the Robber's Cliff? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā sought out the most <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>eminent teachers</b></a> of her time, yet found that none could compete with her in debate until she met Sāriputta? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā gathered a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>large crowd</b></a> of people to witness her debate with Sāriputta, believing that a public audience was necessary for a fair contest? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā was ordained with the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>highest fruit</b></a> of Arahantship already attained, which she achieved while still standing as a laywoman listening to the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā was praised for being an <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>astute woman</b></a> whose quick-wittedness allowed her to perceive the true intentions of those who wished her harm? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā was encouraged by Sāriputta to approach the Buddha, the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>Teacher of Gods and Men</b></a>, to find the answers she sought? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Bhaddā Kuṇḍalakesā realized that the teachings of the Jains were <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato"><b>not special</b></a> after she had spent time learning and practicing their doctrine? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.9/en/sujato">Thig 5.9</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was born in the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Devadaha</b></a> into the family of Mahā-Suppabuddha and shared the same clan name, Gotama, as the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was the younger sister of Queen <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Mahāmāyā</b></a>, who was the mother of the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that when Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was young, fortune-tellers predicted that the children of both her and her sister would become <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Wheel-turning Monarchs</b></a> (Cakkavatti)? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was married to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>King Suddhodana</b></a>, the father of the Buddha, along with her older sister? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was initially <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>refused</b></a> by the Buddha when she first requested permission to enter the monastic life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī demonstrated her deep commitment by <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>cutting her hair</b></a> and putting on ochre robes before leading a large group of women to find the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī traveled to the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Vesālī</b></a> with five hundred other Sakyan women whose husbands had already joined the monastic order? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was eventually allowed to ordain due to the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>intercession of Venerable Ānanda</b></a>, who spoke to the Buddha on behalf of the women? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha established the Bhikkhunī Sangha after Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī agreed to follow the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Eight Respectful Rules</b></a> (Garudhammas)? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī attained the state of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Arahantship</b></a>, the highest stage of enlightenment, characterized by both intuitive and analytical knowledge? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was officially designated by the Buddha as the foremost among all nuns who are <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>long-standing</b></a> and have great experience? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī praised the Buddha as the "Heroic Enlightened One" who had <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>released her from suffering</b></a> and the cycle of rebirth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī realized the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Four Noble Truths</b></a>, which included fully understanding suffering and the cessation of craving? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī described her spiritual victory as having successfully traveled the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>Noble Eightfold Path</b></a> to its final conclusion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī reflected on how she had been a mother, a son, a father, and a brother in her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>previous lives</b></a> throughout the long cycle of saṃsāra? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī declared her current physical existence to be her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>final body</b></a>, signaling the absolute end of birth and death for her? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī urged all disciples of the Buddha to live with <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>diligent effort</b></a> and persistent energy to overcome spiritual obstacles? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī believed that Queen Mahāmāyā gave birth to the Buddha for the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>benefit of many</b></a>, providing a way for people to find relief from sickness and death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī reached a state where all <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>craving</b></a> (taṇhā) had been completely washed away through her spiritual practice? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī was accompanied by five hundred other nuns who attained the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>six higher knowledges</b></a> (chaḷabhiññā) after receiving instruction from the monk Nandaka? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī expressed her gratitude by stating that the Buddha had successfully <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato"><b>dispelled the group of suffering</b></a> for those who were afflicted? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.6/en/sujato">Thig 6.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> was born into a Brahmin family in the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Benares</b></a> and was given her name because of her extraordinary physical beauty? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the spiritual journey of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> was precipitated by the death of her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>younger brother</b></a>, which left her father in a state of overwhelming grief? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the father of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> encountered <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī</b></a> while he was wandering in sorrow, and she shared how she had overcome the loss of hundreds of her own relatives? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī</b> explained to the father of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> that she no longer grieved or wept because she had found the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>way of escape</b></a> from birth and death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b>'s father traveled to the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Mithilā</b></a> specifically to see the Buddha and hear the Dhamma that could end all suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the father of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> heard the Buddha teach the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Four Noble Truths</b></a>, including the origin of suffering and the path to its cessation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b>'s father attained the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>three knowledges</b></a> (tevijjā) only three nights after his ordination as a monk? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that after attaining enlightenment, the father of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> sent his <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>charioteer</b></a> back home to inform his family of his spiritual success and renunciation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the mother of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> was so pleased to hear of her husband's attainment that she offered the charioteer a reward of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>one thousand pieces of gold</b></a> and the chariot itself? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the charioteer of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b>'s family refused the gold and the chariot, choosing instead to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>go forth</b></a> into the homeless life himself? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that when <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> heard of her father's renunciation, she told her mother that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>wealth</b></a> meant nothing to her and that she also wished to ordain? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the mother of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> initially tried to persuade her to stay by offering her a vast inheritance of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>elephants, cattle, and gold</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> rejected her family fortune, viewing it as a source of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>grief and affliction</b></a> rather than a benefit? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the mother of <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> eventually granted her permission to ordain, wishing that her daughter would <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>destroy the taints</b></a> (āsavas) in the life to come? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b>'s mother encouraged her to live a simple life, surviving on <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>almsfood</b></a> and wearing robes made of cast-off rags? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> attained Arahantship and mastered the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>analytical knowledges</b></a> (paṭisambhidā) shortly after joining the Order? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> cultivated the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>divine eye</b></a> (dibba-cakkhu), allowing her to see the passing away and rebirth of beings? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> was able to recall her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>past lives</b></a>, understanding exactly where she had lived in previous existences? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> expressed deep gratitude toward her teacher, whom she called a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>good friend</b></a> and a source of great brilliance? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> traveled from Benares to the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Sāvatthī</b></a> to announce her attainment of enlightenment to the Buddha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> sought to "roar a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>lion's roar</b></a>" in the presence of the Buddha to declare her final liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> described the Buddha’s physical appearance as being like <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>pure gold</b></a>, radiant and beautiful? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> praised the Buddha as the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>tamer of the untamed</b></a>, who possessed total fearlessness and supreme awakening? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> referred to herself as a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>daughter born of the mouth</b></a> of the Buddha, signifying her spiritual birth through his teachings? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> declared that she was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>born of the Dhamma</b></a> and had successfully completed all the tasks required for liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> asserted that she was completely <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>free from taints</b></a> and had severed all ties and attachments to the world? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha welcomed <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b></a> upon her arrival, acknowledging that her journey through the cycle of birth and death was finally at an end? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> described the Buddha as a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Great Hero</b></a> (Mahāvīra) and prostrated at his feet as his devoted disciple? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that after <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> and her father ordained, her mother and all their <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>household servants</b></a> eventually followed them into the religious life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> emphasized that through her practice, the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>Buddha's teaching</b></a> had been fully accomplished in her life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> characterized herself as being without <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>clinging or substrate</b></a>, having reached the ultimate state of dispassion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Sundarī</b> attained the same <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato"><b>three knowledges</b></a> as her father, demonstrating the effectiveness of the Buddha's path for both men and women? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.4/en/sujato">Thig 13.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Muttā was encouraged by the Buddha to be like the moon released from the mouth of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato"><b>Rāhu</b></a>, a metaphor for achieving total freedom from all spiritual bonds? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato">Thig 1.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Muttā, having attained a liberated mind, was told by the Buddha that she could now enjoy her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato"><b>almsfood</b></a> without the burden of any spiritual debt? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato">Thig 1.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Muttā was the daughter of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato"><b>renowned Brahmin</b></a> in the city of Sāvatthī before she decided to renounce the household life at the age of twenty? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato">Thig 1.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Muttā entered the monastic order under the spiritual guidance of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato"><b>Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī</b></a>, the first Bhikkhuni and the Buddha's aunt? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato">Thig 1.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that while Bhikkhuni Muttā was meditating in a secluded spot, the Buddha appeared before her in a vision of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato"><b>radiance</b></a> to deliver a verse that helped her attain Arahantship? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato">Thig 1.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Muttā valued her verse of awakening so highly that she recited it again as she was <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato"><b>about to pass away</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.2/en/sujato">Thig 1.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Puṇṇā, whose name means "<a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato"><b>full</b></a>," was exhorted by the Buddha to become full of the Dhamma just like the moon on the fifteenth day? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato">Thig 1.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Puṇṇā was born into the family of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato"><b>wealthy merchant</b></a> in Sāvatthī but chose to leave behind her riches for the life of a renunciant? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato">Thig 1.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Puṇṇā achieved the highest spiritual realization by using her wisdom to shatter the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato"><b>mass of darkness</b></a> that represents ignorance and delusion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato">Thig 1.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Puṇṇā felt inspired to go forth into the homeless life after hearing a profound <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato"><b>Dhamma teaching</b></a> given by Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.3/en/sujato">Thig 1.3</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā belonged to a noble <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato"><b>Sakyan family</b></a> in the city of Kapilavatthu before she joined the monastic order? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato">Thig 1.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā had been a member of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato"><b>inner court</b></a> of the Bodhisatta before his Great Renunciation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato">Thig 1.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā was urged by the Buddha to train herself diligently in the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato"><b>higher trainings</b></a> so that no spiritual bonds could ever overcome her? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato">Thig 1.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā attained a state where she could live in the world completely free from all <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato"><b>taints</b></a> (āsavas) of the mind? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato">Thig 1.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā was described as having accumulated <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato"><b>merit</b></a> under many previous Buddhas, which prepared her for liberation in her final life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato">Thig 1.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā was instructed to live <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato"><b>unattached</b></a> to all worldly things, ensuring that no yokes or ties could bind her to the cycle of suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.4/en/sujato">Thig 1.4</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that a second Bhikkhuni named Tissā was exhorted to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato"><b>yoke her mind</b></a> firmly to the Dhamma to prevent it from wandering into unwholesome states? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato">Thig 1.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā (the second) was warned by the Buddha not to let the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato"><b>opportune moment</b></a> for spiritual practice pass her by? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato">Thig 1.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā (the second) learned that those who miss their chance for liberation will <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato"><b>sorrow</b></a> deeply when they eventually fall into the realms of hell? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato">Thig 1.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Tissā (the second) was advised to maintain a constant <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato"><b>focus</b></a> on wholesome phenomena, never letting even a single second be wasted? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.5/en/sujato">Thig 1.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhīrā was exhorted to experience the state of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato"><b>cessation</b></a>, which refers to the ending of all mental and physical suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato">Thig 1.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhīrā attained spiritual tranquility through the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato"><b>stilling of thoughts</b></a> and the elimination of mental proliferation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato">Thig 1.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhīrā realized that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato"><b>true bliss</b></a> is found in the calm that comes when all mental distractions have been pacified? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato">Thig 1.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhīrā directed her mind toward Nibbāna, which is described as the supreme <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato"><b>security from the yoke</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato">Thig 1.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhīrā was encouraged to touch the "unconditioned," a state that is <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato"><b>not subject to change</b></a> or impermanence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato">Thig 1.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhīrā was told that by inclining her mind toward Nibbāna, she would reach a state that is <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato"><b>peaceful</b></a> and secure from all worldly dangers? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato">Thig 1.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Dhīrā's spiritual journey involved mastering the ability to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato"><b>feel</b></a> the subtle peace that arises from the cessation of all cravings? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig1.6/en/sujato">Thig 1.6</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī was born into a wealthy <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>Brahmin family</b></a> of the Kosiya clan in the city of Sāgala before she chose to renounce the world? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī was once the wife of a nobleman named Pippali, who later became the renowned Elder <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>Mahākassapa</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī demonstrated her detachment by handing over all her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>wealth and property</b></a> to her relatives when her husband decided to ordain? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī spent <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>five years</b></a> living at Titthiyārāma before she was finally able to receive full ordination from Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī was declared by the Buddha to be the foremost among all bhikkhunis in the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>recollection of past lives</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī described herself as a true heir of the Buddha who had mastered the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>Triple Knowledge</b></a> and conquered the fear of death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī attained the state of an Arahant by developing <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>insight meditation</b></a> and seeing the inherent danger in worldly existence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī successfully defeated <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>Mara’s army</b></a> and proclaimed that she now bears her final body, marking the end of her rebirth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī and Elder Mahākassapa both achieved a state where their mental taints were destroyed, leaving them <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>cooled and quenched</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī praised Elder Mahākassapa for his exceptional <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>meditative absorption</b></a> and his ability to see into both divine and hellish realms? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī stated that a person who possesses the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>Triple Knowledge</b></a> is the only one who truly deserves the spiritual title of a Brahmin? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Bhaddā Kapilānī was formally ordained by the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato"><b>Great Mother Mahāpajāpatī</b></a> after she moved to the monastery from Titthiyārāma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig4.1/en/sujato">Thig 4.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī was born in the town of Devadaha and originally served as the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>nurse</b></a> for the Buddha's foster mother, Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī struggled for <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>twenty-five years</b></a> following her ordination without experiencing even a single moment of mental peace or concentration? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī was so persistently obsessed by <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>sensual desire</b></a> that her mind remained completely uncomposed for over two decades? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī reached a point of deep spiritual despair and <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>wept with her arms raised</b></a> before entering her dwelling to find a way to tame her mind? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī sought out the guidance of the eminent Bhikkhuni <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>Dhammadinnā</b></a> to help her overcome the mental defilements that blocked her progress? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī achieved her final spiritual breakthrough after receiving instructions on the nature of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>aggregates, sense bases, and elements</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī attained the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>Six Direct Knowledges</b></a>, which represent the highest level of supernormal powers and spiritual realization? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī declared that she had successfully completed the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>Buddha's teaching</b></a> after achieving the final destruction of all her mental taints? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī used her newly acquired <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>divine eye</b></a> to see into her own past lives and understand the nature of the past? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī purified her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>divine ear element</b></a>, which allowed her to perceive sounds that are beyond the reach of normal human hearing? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī attained the supernormal power to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>know the minds of others</b></a> as part of her complete spiritual liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vaḍḍhesī emphasized that she only attained <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato"><b>liberation</b></a> after her heart finally turned away from all worldly desires through the power of the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.1/en/sujato">Thig 5.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs were once women from wealthy families who sought out Bhikkhunī Paṭācārā because they were overwhelmed by grief after the loss of their <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>dead sons</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs learned from their teacher that grieving for a child is futile because one does not know the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>unknown path</b></a> by which a being arrives at birth or departs at death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs were taught that a being comes into a family <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>uninvited</b></a> from another state of existence and leaves without requesting permission when their time is up? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs realized that it is the nature of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>conditioned beings</b></a> to come from one place and depart to another, making lamentation over their passing unnecessary? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs reflected on the teaching that a child is only allowed to stay for a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>certain number of days</b></a> before continuing their journey through the cycle of rebirth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs understood that since a being arrives by one path and departs by a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>different path</b></a>, there is no logical reason to weep for them after they have passed away? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that after listening to the Dhamma, the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs were so moved that they chose to enter the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>homeless life</b></a> under the guidance of Bhikkhunī Paṭācārā? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs diligently practiced insight meditation until they <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>attained Arahantship</b></a>, achieving the highest goal of the spiritual life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs described their liberation as having finally removed the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>arrow of grief</b></a> that had been deeply embedded in their hearts? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs achieved a state of peace <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>without longing</b></a> after they successfully uprooted the sorrow that had once obsessed them? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs declared their spiritual security by taking refuge in the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>Triple Gem</b></a> of the Buddha, the Dhamma, and the Sangha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that because they were so proficient in the instructions of their mentor, this group of women became known throughout the community as the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>dependents of Paṭācārā</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī was born into a noble family in the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>Vesālī</b></a> and lived a happy life with her husband before tragedy struck? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī was driven to a state of madness and mental derangement after her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>toddler son</b></a> unexpectedly died? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that in her state of extreme grief, Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī wandered aimlessly for <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>three years</b></a>, completely losing her sense of self and purpose? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that during her period of madness, Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī wandered through the streets <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>naked and disheveled</b></a>, with her hair in total disarray? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that for years, Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī lived in the most desolate places, such as <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>garbage heaps</b></a>, cemeteries, and roadsides, while suffering in her mental turmoil? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī endured extreme physical hardship, including <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>hunger and thirst</b></a>, while she roamed the countryside as a madwoman? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī’s life changed forever when she reached the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>Mithilā</b></a> and encountered the Buddha walking on the road? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī described the Buddha as the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>Self-tamed One</b></a> who had total mastery over his senses and was completely free from fear? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī was able to regain her composure and sanity simply by coming into the presence and the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>power of the Buddha</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī felt that she had received <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>Gotama's compassion</b></a> when he took pity on her condition and preached the Dhamma to her? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that after hearing the Buddha's brief discourse, Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī immediately requested to go forth and was accepted into the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>homeless life</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī achieved ultimate liberation by practicing <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>insight meditation</b></a> with great effort until her wisdom had fully matured? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī declared that she had reached the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>secure state</b></a> of Nibbāna, where all her suffering was permanently extinguished? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī achieved a profound realization where she <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>understood the root</b></a> from which all sorrow and mental distress are born? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vāsiṭṭhī praised the Buddha as the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato"><b>Fearless One</b></a> because he had conquered all birth and death through his enlightenment? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.2/en/sujato">Thig 6.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs emphasized that because they followed the teacher's advice, they were able to see the nature of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>coming and going</b></a> that applies to all living things? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Five Hundred Bhikkhunīs found a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato"><b>peaceful state</b></a> of mind that was no longer disturbed by the loss of loved ones after they realized the truth of the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.1/en/sujato">Thig 6.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>Guttā</b></a>, a Bhikkhunī born into a Brahmin family in Sāvatthī, chose to renounce the world for the supreme goal, even though it meant abandoning her children and her old life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Guttā entered the monastic life under the spiritual leadership of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī</b></a>, the first nun of the Buddhist Sangha? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that despite her deep faith, Bhikkhunī Guttā initially struggled with her practice because her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>mind</b></a> would frequently wander toward external objects? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha intervened to encourage Bhikkhunī Guttā by <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>projecting a radiance</b></a> and appearing before her in a vision to deliver a teaching on mental restraint? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha warned Bhikkhunī Guttā that the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>deceptive mind</b></a> delights in the domain of Māra and causes beings to wander through many lives in a state of delusion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Guttā was instructed by the Buddha to abandon the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>lower fetters</b></a> (saṃyojana), which include sensual desire, ill will, personality view, grasping at precepts and vows, and doubt? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha promised Bhikkhunī Guttā that by abandoning specific mental shackles, she would reach a state where she would <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>never return</b></a> to this world of rebirth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Guttā was urged to cut through the higher fetters of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>conceit, ignorance, and restlessness</b></a> to finally bring her cycle of suffering to an end? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Guttā reached a state of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato"><b>perfect peace</b></a> (anupabbajja) after she fully understood the nature of rebirth and abandoned all worldly desires? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.7/en/sujato">Thig 6.7</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>Vijayā</b></a>, a Bhikkhunī born in Rājagaha, was a close lay friend of the great nun Khemā before she decided to follow her into the monastic life? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā was inspired to ordain after reflecting that if a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>queen</b></a> like Khemā could renounce her royal life, then she, a commoner, should be able to do so as well? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā's spiritual journey was motivated by deep contemplation on the universal suffering inherent in <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>birth, aging, sickness, and death</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā initially found it so difficult to control her mind that she <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>left her cell</b></a> four or five times because she could not find any tranquility? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā sought instruction from a senior nun to discuss the Dhamma, specifically asking about the nature of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>elements and sense bases</b></a> (dhātu and āyatana)? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā achieved her spiritual breakthrough after receiving guidance on the Four Noble Truths, the spiritual faculties, and the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>powers</b></a> (bala) of a practitioner? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā practiced the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>Seven Factors of Enlightenment</b></a> (bojjhaṅga) as a means to reach the supreme goal of Nibbāna? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that during the first watch of the night she attained Arahantship, Bhikkhunī Vijayā was able to remember her many <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>previous lives</b></a> in the cycle of saṃsāra? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that in the middle watch of the night, Bhikkhunī Vijayā purified her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>divine eye</b></a> (dibbacakkhu), allowing her to see the rebirth of other beings according to their kamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that in the last watch of the night, Bhikkhunī Vijayā completely shattered the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>mass of darkness</b></a>, referring to the spiritual ignorance that binds beings to suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that upon her enlightenment, Bhikkhunī Vijayā experienced a profound sense of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>spiritual joy</b></a> that pervaded her entire physical body? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā attained full liberation on the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>seventh night</b></a> of her intensive practice, after which she finally relaxed her body in peace? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā attained Arahantship along with the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>analytical knowledges</b></a> (paṭisambhidā) of the Dhamma and its profound meaning? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhunī Vijayā described the result of her training as having correctly followed the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato"><b>Noble Eightfold Path</b></a> to its ultimate conclusion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig6.8/en/sujato">Thig 6.8</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> was the daughter of a wealthy goldsmith in the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>Rājagaha</b></a> before she renounced the world? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> was given her name, which means "beautiful," because of her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>extraordinary appearance</b></a> when she reached adulthood? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> attained the fruit of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>Stream-enterer</b></a> (sotāpanna) immediately after hearing the Buddha preach the Four Noble Truths? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> chose to renounce her household life and ordain under the leadership of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>Mahāpajāpatī Gotamī</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> had to defend her decision to remain a nun when her relatives tried to entice her back to the world by highlighting the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>attractions of life</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> delivered twenty-four verses of Dhamma to her relatives to cure them of their <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>ambition and desire</b></a> for worldly things? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> renounced a vast inheritance that included servants, laborers, and <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>fertile lands</b></a> in order to seek spiritual liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> argued that gold and silver cannot lead one to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>enlightenment or peace</b></a> and are unsuitable for the life of a recluse? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> taught that worldly riches are not the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>noble wealth</b></a> (ariya dhana) of those who seek the truth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> warned that gold and silver only serve to increase <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>greed and delusion</b></a> and foster mental stains? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> characterized material wealth as being filled with <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>danger and anxiety</b></a>, noting that nothing in it is permanent? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> observed how people who are obsessed with wealth end up <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>fighting and opposing</b></a> one another, leading to broad social conflict? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> pointed out that those who sink into sensual pleasures face many disasters, including <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>killing, binding, and torture</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> told her relatives they were acting like <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>enemies</b></a> by trying to bind her back into the cycle of sensual pleasures? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> realized that gold and silver have no power to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>sever the taints</b></a> (āsavas) of the mind? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> compared sensual pleasures to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>arrows and bonds</b></a> that keep a person trapped in suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> expressed her commitment to the holy life by shaving her head and wearing the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>great robe</b></a> of a monastic? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> preferred the life of a homeless wanderer, sustaining herself through <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>almsfood</b></a> and wearing robes made from discarded rags? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> renounced both human and heavenly pleasures in order to abide in <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>unshakeable bliss</b></a> and liberation? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> compared sensual desire to a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>pit of fire</b></a>, warning that there is no true safety to be found within it? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> described the path of craving as a rough and <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>thorny road</b></a> leading into a vast wilderness of delusion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> likened sensual pleasures to the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>head of a snake</b></a>, a danger that only the foolish and blind enjoy? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> stated that those who do not understand the Dhamma are drowning in <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>muddy silt</b></a> and cannot see the end of birth and death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> taught that sensual desire leads people down a path toward <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>evil states</b></a> of existence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> observed that sensual pleasures can cause a person to become <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>insane and disordered</b></a> in their thinking? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> warned that those who indulge in sensual desire are about to fall into the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>trap of Māra</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> emphasized that sensual pleasure offers only <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>little sweetness</b></a> while creating great struggle and suffering? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> resolved to follow the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>Eightfold Path</b></a>, which she described as straight, safe, and free from sorrow? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> achieved the state of an Arahant on the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>eighth day</b></a> following her ordination? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> was mentored and instructed by the Great Disciple <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>Uppalavaṇṇā</b></a> during her early days in the Order? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> attained the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>three knowledges</b></a> (tevijjā) and completely overcame the power of death? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that <b>Sakka</b>, the king of the devas, was said to have come with a host of celestial beings to <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato"><b>pay homage</b></a> to <b>Bhikkhunī Subhā</b> after her enlightenment? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5/en/sujato">Thig 13.5</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā, a princess of the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>Sakya clan</b></a> born in Kapilavatthu, was initially so proud of her beauty that she avoided meeting the Buddha for fear of being rebuked? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā was known by the name "Abhirūpā Nandā" because of her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>exquisite physical form</b></a>, which she valued so highly that it became a spiritual obstacle? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that the Buddha used his psychic powers to show Bhikkhuni Nandā a vision of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>beautiful woman aging</b></a> and becoming decrepit to shock her into realizing the impermanent nature of the body? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā was exhorted by the Buddha to view the human body as a site of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>disease and impurity</b></a>, rather than a source of vanity or pride? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā was instructed by the Buddha to develop <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>one-pointedness of mind</b></a> through the meditation on the foulness of the body to achieve spiritual composure? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā attained the state of an Arahant after being told to cultivate the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>signless meditation</b></a>, which allowed her to uproot the underlying tendency toward conceit? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā only entered the monastic life after her intended husband, Carabhūta, passed away and her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>parents pressured</b></a> her to seek ordination? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā was warned by the Buddha that her heart would only find <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>tranquil peace</b></a> once she had abandoned the subtle conceit of self through direct knowledge? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā was born into a distinguished family in the city of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>Kosambī</b></a> and sought refuge in the Sangha following the tragic death of her dear friend Sāmāvatī? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā struggled for a long time to attain the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>Noble Path</b></a> because her mind was overwhelmed by the intense grief she felt for her deceased companion? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā finally attained the "Dhamma-eye" after being moved by a sermon delivered by <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>Venerable Ānanda</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā reached the stage of an Arahant and realized the highest truth just <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>seven days</b></a> after her first major breakthrough in understanding? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā reflected that she had entered and left her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>meditation dwelling</b></a> four or five times without finding any composure before she finally succeeded? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā achieved her ultimate spiritual liberation on the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>eighth night</b></a> of her intensive practice, at which point all craving was completely uprooted? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā declared she had successfully fulfilled the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>Buddha's teaching</b></a> by striving with a mind that was no longer prone to distraction? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Sāmā’s early monastic life was hindered by an <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato"><b>inability to control</b></a> the sorrow that arose from her worldly attachments to her friends? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.10/en/sujato">Thig 2.10</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Jentī was born into the royal <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato"><b>Licchavi family</b></a> in the city of Vesālī before renouncing her status to follow the Buddha’s path? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato">Thig 2.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Jentī attained the fruit of Arahantship while listening to the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato"><b>Buddha's teaching</b></a>, which led her to reflect deeply on the change within her own heart? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato">Thig 2.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Jentī proclaimed that she had successfully cultivated the <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato"><b>Seven Factors of Enlightenment</b></a> as the direct way to reach the state of Nibbāna? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato">Thig 2.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Jentī announced that the cycle of rebirth was ended for her, declaring that she was now dwelling in her <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato"><b>final body</b></a>? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato">Thig 2.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Jentī rejoiced in the realization that there would be <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato"><b>no further rebirth</b></a> for her because she had completely severed the bonds of existence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.2/en/sujato">Thig 2.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā's path to enlightenment began when she was forced to see that even a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>beautiful body</b></a> is subject to being broken, foul, and full of disease? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
