<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Nandā was told by the Buddha to regard the body as <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato"><b>rotting and foul</b></a> in order to reach a state of mental composure and one-pointedness? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig2.1/en/sujato">Thig 2.1</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā was born in the city of Vesālī as the daughter of a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>courtesan</b></a> before she eventually renounced that lifestyle to seek the Dhamma? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā admitted she was once intoxicated by her own <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>beauty and youth</b></a>, which led her to hold others in deep contempt? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā once attempted to seduce the eminent Elder <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>Mahā Moggallāna</b></a> while he was walking on his alms round in Vesālī? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā was converted to the path of renunciation after being <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>rebuked</b></a> by the Elder Mahā Moggallāna for her improper behavior and impure thoughts? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā compared her former life of enticing men at a "shop of beauty" to a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>hunter</b></a> setting out a snare for unsuspecting prey? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā described her past use of elaborate jewelry and provocative poses as <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>tricks</b></a> designed specifically to mock and allure "fools"? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā eventually achieved the final goal of <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>Arahantship</b></a> after joining the Sangha and practicing with great diligence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā declared that she now dwells in a state of peace, having attained <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>concentration without thought-directedness</b></a> while meditating under a tree? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā successfully severed all <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>fetters</b></a> and "yokes" that bind a person to both the human and divine realms of existence? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā used the term <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>cooled</b></a> to describe her spiritual state after quenching the internal fires of passion and desire? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā completely discarded all <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>taints</b></a> of the mind, which include sensual desire, the desire for existence, and ignorance? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā traded her luxurious jewelry and finery for a <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>shaved head</b></a> and the simple, dusty robes of a homeless renunciant? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā claimed she had formerly been obsessed with her own <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>fame and renown</b></a> before discovering the true value of the Buddha's teaching? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
<div class="quote-entry"><p><b>#DidYouKnow</b> that Bhikkhuni Vimalā lived a life of humble <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato"><b>alms-seeking</b></a> after letting go of her former life of vanity and material wealth? <a href="https://suttacentral.net/thig5.2/en/sujato">Thig 5.2</a></p></div><hr>
